From 6cb26284a89aa6190374224bd027fdf404b79802 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:43:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: type Avalanche proof and peer-file lifecycle events

Convert 11 debug producers, retaining Avalanche category, proof-id hash semantics, paths, counted peers, copy-before-return exception detail, unchanged proof pools, file formats and reconciliation. Existing typed events remain untouched.

Scripted diff commands:
/private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/convert.py --root . --rules contrib/logging/conversion/rules/avalanche-peer-lifecycle-diagnostics.json --report /private/tmp/logging-core-avalanche-report.json --apply
git clang-format --force --binary /opt/homebrew/bin/clang-format --style "{BasedOnStyle: InheritParentConfig, BreakStringLiterals: false}" HEAD -- src/avalanche/peermanager.cpp src/avalanche/processor.cpp
python3 test/lint/lint-log-events.py src/avalanche/peermanager.cpp src/avalanche/processor.cpp
git diff --check

Source-only: NOT_COMPILED / NOT_RUN. No new API, protocol, file format or producer-private test scaffolding. Reuse peer persistence and proof-pool tests when runtime ownership is released.
---
